@* MobileSaleDetail.razor — mobile version of the SaleDetail (order detail) page.
   Route: /m/Sales/{SaleId}
   Layout: MobileLayout

   PORTS the desktop SaleDetail.razor features into a mobile-friendly
   single-column layout:
     - Page header with back button + sale display number + inline
       status badge subtitle.
     - Large status banner (color-coded by status — Draft / Pending /
       Approved / Invoiced / Cancelled) using the desktop's
       `.status-bg-*` color tokens so the colors read identically on
       mobile and desktop.
     - Sale meta info summary card (customer name, audit-trail
       timestamps for created / submitted / approved / invoiced /
       cancelled, with the audit-actor line on the Created entry).
     - Line items list (one .m-list-item per sale line — clickable
       product name → /m/Products/{ProductId} when ProductId is
       available, qty, unit price, line total) formatted as Toman via
       the local FormatMoney helper (IRR / 10 → Toman, matching the
       MobileSales list page so a sale reads the same on the list and
       the detail page).
     - Total card with grand total (FormatMoney) + line count + total
       units.
     - Staff-only action buttons (Approve when Pending, Mark as
       Invoiced when Approved, Cancel when Pending/Approved) — Cancel
       uses an inline textarea confirmation form (mirrors
       MobileCart's _confirmingClear pattern) for the cancellation
       reason. ReadOnly and Customer roles don't see the action stack
       at all; the backend enforces [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager,
       Admin)] on each command as defense-in-depth.
     - Loading → error → not-found → content state machine (matches
       the MobileProducts / MobileSales gold-standard pattern).

   BACKEND CONTRACT (same as desktop SaleDetail.razor):
     - Load: GetSaleByIdQuery { SaleId } → Result<SaleDto>. The handler
       resolves the current user server-side and rejects customers
       trying to view other users' sales with a generic "not found"
       message (avoids leaking existence).
     - Approve (staff only): ApproveSaleCommand(SaleId) → Result.
       Pending → Approved. Decrements stock per line.
       [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].
     - Mark as invoiced (staff only): MarkAsInvoicedCommand(SaleId) →
       Result. Approved → Invoiced (terminal).
       [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].
     - Cancel (staff only): CancelSaleCommand(SaleId, Reason) →
       Result. Reachable from Pending or Approved (NOT Draft — use
       delete-draft via /m/Cart; NOT Invoiced — credit note flow).
       Reason is required (3-500 chars; enforced by validator).
       [RequireRoles(Employee, Manager, Admin)].

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN (matches desktop SaleDetail.razor):
     _canActOnSales is computed in OnInitializedAsync via
     AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync() (NOT via
     ICurrentUserService.IsInRole). Reason: ICurrentUserService in
     Blazor Server resolves from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext,
     which is only populated during the INITIAL prerender request —
     null over the SignalR circuit afterwards. AuthStateProvider is
     the canonical source of role info for interactive components.
     ICurrentUserService IS still safe inside Wolverine handlers
     (where the message bus sets up its own ambient context) — just
     not in the Blazor UI layer for first-render visibility checks.

   MONEY: FormatMoney mirrors the MobileSales list-page helper (IRR
   is divided by 10 and labelled "تومان"; non-IRR currencies pass
   through with their currency code). This means the detail page's
   grand total reads the SAME as the list page's row total —
   consistent UX. (The desktop SaleDetail uses FormatMoneyRial which
   keeps IRR as ریال — mobile deliberately uses Toman for parity with
   the rest of the mobile surface area.)

   TIMEZONE: FormatTimestamp delegates to CultureFormat.FormatTehranDateTime
   (Tehran UTC+3:30, no DST since 2022; Jalali calendar + Persian
   digits in fa-IR mode, Gregorian + ASCII in en-US).
*@

@page "/m/Sales/{SaleId:guid}"
@attribute [Authorize]
@layout TakOne.WebUI.Components.Layout.MobileLayout.MobileLayout
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Localization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Errors
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Queries.GetSaleById
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.ApproveSale
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.MarkAsInvoiced
@using TakOne.Application.Sales.Commands.CancelSale
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<MobileSaleDetail> Loc
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider

<PageTitle>@(_sale is null ? Loc["PageTitle"] : $"{CultureFormat.FormatDigits(_sale.DisplayNumber)} — {Loc["PageTitle"]}")</PageTitle>

@if (_isLoading)
{
    <div class="m-loading">
        <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false" Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate" Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Medium" />
        <p>@Loc["Loading"]</p>
    </div>
}
else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
{
    <div class="m-error-box">
        <p>@_loadError</p>
        <button class="m-btn m-btn-secondary" @onclick="LoadSaleAsync">@Loc["RetryButton"]</button>
    </div>
}
else if (_sale is null)
{
    @* Not-found / not-allowed: the handler returns Result.Failure with a
       "not found" message for both genuinely-missing sales AND sales the
       caller isn't allowed to see (defense-in-depth — never leak that the
       sale exists). Either way the user sees the same friendly message. *@
    <div class="m-empty">
        <p>@Loc["NotFoundMessage"]</p>
        <button class="m-btn m-btn-secondary" @onclick="GoToSales">@Loc["BackToList"]</button>
    </div>
}
else
{
    @* ── 1. Page header — back button + sale number + inline status badge.
           The .m-page-header-back wrapper + .m-back-btn class are mobile-
           detail-specific; the orchestrator adds them to mobile.css in a
           later pass (until then, the page renders unstyled-but-functional). *@
    <div class="m-page-header-back">
        <button type="button"
                class="m-back-btn"
                aria-label="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                title="@Loc["BackToList"]"
                @onclick="GoToSales">
            <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" />
            </svg>
        </button>
        <div class="m-page-header-text">
            <h1 class="m-page-title">@CultureFormat.ToCultureDigits(_sale.DisplayNumber)</h1>
            <p class="m-page-subtitle">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.CreatedAtUtc)</p>
        </div>
        <span class="m-badge @GetStatusBadgeClass(_sale.Status)">@GetStatusLabel(_sale.Status)</span>
    </div>

    @* ── 2. Large status banner — color-coded by status. Uses the desktop's
           status-bg-* color tokens (rgba background + matching foreground)
           so a status reads identically on mobile and desktop. The
           orchestrator adds the .m-status-banner + per-status CSS classes
           in a later pass; until then the inline class names match the
           desktop SaleDetail.razor's HeadContent <style> block (those styles
           are page-scoped on desktop but won't leak to mobile — they're
           defined inside desktop's <HeadContent>, so the mobile page just
           needs its own equivalent classes; orchestrator adds them). *@
    <div class="m-status-banner @GetStatusBannerClass(_sale.Status)">
        <span class="m-status-banner-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            @GetStatusIcon(_sale.Status)
        </span>
        <span class="m-status-banner-label">@GetStatusLabel(_sale.Status)</span>
    </div>

    @* ── 3. Cancellation reason panel — only shown when the sale is
           Cancelled and a reason was recorded. Mirrors the desktop's
           .cancellation-reason panel (italic, danger-tinted). *@
    @if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Cancelled)
         && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_sale.CancellationReason))
    {
        <div class="m-cancellation-reason">
            <div class="m-cancellation-reason-label">@Loc["CancellationReasonLabel"]</div>
            <p class="m-cancellation-reason-text">@_sale.CancellationReason</p>
        </div>
    }

    @* ── 4. Sale meta info — customer + audit trail. One .m-summary-card
           with .m-summary-row entries. Rows with no timestamp (e.g. a
           pending sale that hasn't been approved yet) show "—" muted. *@
    <div class="m-summary-card">
        <div class="m-summary-row">
            <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["ColCustomer"]</span>
            <span class="m-summary-value">@_sale.CustomerName</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m-summary-row">
            <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditCreated"]</span>
            <span class="m-summary-value">
                @FormatTimestamp(_sale.CreatedAtUtc)
                <span class="m-summary-audit-actor">@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["AuditByFormat"], _sale.CreatedByName)</span>
            </span>
        </div>
        @if (_sale.SubmittedAtUtc.HasValue)
        {
            <div class="m-summary-row">
                <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditSubmitted"]</span>
                <span class="m-summary-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.SubmittedAtUtc.Value)</span>
            </div>
        }
        @if (_sale.ApprovedAtUtc.HasValue)
        {
            <div class="m-summary-row">
                <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditApproved"]</span>
                <span class="m-summary-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.ApprovedAtUtc.Value)</span>
            </div>
        }
        else if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Pending))
        {
            <div class="m-summary-row">
                <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditApproved"]</span>
                <span class="m-summary-value m-summary-value-pending">@Loc["AuditPending"]</span>
            </div>
        }
        @if (_sale.InvoicedAtUtc.HasValue)
        {
            <div class="m-summary-row">
                <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditInvoiced"]</span>
                <span class="m-summary-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.InvoicedAtUtc.Value)</span>
            </div>
        }
        @if (_sale.CancelledAtUtc.HasValue)
        {
            <div class="m-summary-row">
                <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["AuditCancelled"]</span>
                <span class="m-summary-value">@FormatTimestamp(_sale.CancelledAtUtc.Value)</span>
            </div>
        }
    </div>

    @* ── 5. Line items list — one .m-list-item per sale line. Each shows
           the product name (clickable → /m/Products/{ProductId} when
           ProductId is not Guid.Empty; non-clickable for legacy lines
           without a ProductId), the line # prefix, the quantity, the unit
           price, and the line total. All money values are formatted via
           FormatMoney (IRR / 10 → Toman, matching the MobileSales list). *@
    <div class="m-list">
        @if (_sale.LineItems.Count == 0)
        {
            <p class="m-empty">@Loc["NoLineItems"]</p>
        }
        else
        {
            @foreach (var line in _sale.LineItems)
            {
                var l = line;  // closure-capture for the click handler
                var canOpenProduct = l.ProductId != Guid.Empty;
                <div class="m-list-item">
                    <div class="m-list-item-main">
                        <div class="m-list-item-title-row">
                            <span class="m-list-item-line-num">#@CultureFormat.FormatDigits(l.LineNumber)</span>
                            @if (canOpenProduct)
                            {
                                <span class="m-list-item-title m-list-item-title-link"
                                      role="link"
                                      tabindex="0"
                                      @onclick="() => GoToProduct(l.ProductId)">
                                    @l.ProductName
                                </span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <span class="m-list-item-title">@l.ProductName</span>
                            }
                        </div>
                        <div class="m-list-item-subtitle">@Loc["ColQuantity"]: @CultureFormat.FormatNumber(l.Quantity)</div>
                        <div class="m-list-item-subtitle">@Loc["ColUnitPrice"]: @FormatMoney(l.UnitPrice)</div>
                        <div class="m-list-item-meta">
                            <span class="m-list-item-line-total">@Loc["ColLineTotal"]: <strong>@FormatMoney(l.LineTotal)</strong></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
        }
    </div>

    @* ── 6. Total card — grand total + line count + total units. *@
    <div class="m-summary-card">
        <div class="m-summary-row">
            <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["TotalLines"]</span>
            <span class="m-summary-value">@CultureFormat.FormatNumber(_sale.LineItems.Count)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m-summary-row">
            <span class="m-summary-label">@Loc["TotalUnits"]</span>
            <span class="m-summary-value">@CultureFormat.FormatNumber(_sale.LineItems.Sum(li => li.Quantity))</span>
        </div>
        <div class="m-summary-divider"></div>
        <div class="m-summary-row">
            <span class="m-summary-label m-summary-total-label">@Loc["GrandTotal"]</span>
            <span class="m-summary-total">@FormatMoney(_sale.Total)</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    @* ── 7. Staff-only action buttons.
           Visible only to Employee/Manager/Admin (matches the
           [RequireRoles] on each command). ReadOnly + Customer can view
           the sale but can't mutate it — the action stack isn't rendered
           for them at all (defense-in-depth: the handlers also reject
           unauthorized dispatches server-side).

           Approve: enabled only when the sale is Pending.
           Mark as invoiced: enabled only when the sale is Approved.
           Cancel: enabled only when the sale is Pending or Approved.
             First click opens the inline cancel form (textarea + Discard/
             Confirm buttons) — mobile-friendly equivalent of the desktop's
             two-step Radzen-dialog + countdown flow. The inline pattern
             matches MobileCart's _confirmingClear UX. *@
    @if (_canActOnSales)
    {
        <div class="m-action-stack">
            @if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_actionError))
            {
                <div class="m-action-error">
                    <p>@_actionError</p>
                </div>
            }

            @if (_showCancelForm)
            {
                @* Inline cancel form — replaces the Cancel button while
                   _showCancelForm is true. User enters a reason, then clicks
                   Confirm to dispatch CancelSaleCommand (with the 3-500 char
                   length check as defense-in-depth). Discard closes the form
                   without action. *@
                <div class="m-cancel-form">
                    <div class="m-cancel-form-heading">
                        <svg fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" style="width: 1.125rem; height: 1.125rem;">
                            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12 9v3.75m-9.303 3.376c-.866 1.5.217 3.374 1.948 3.374h14.71c1.732 0 2.815-1.873 1.949-3.374L13.949 3.378c-.866-1.5-3.032-1.5-3.898 0L2.697 16.126zM12 15.75h.008v.008H12v-.008z" />
                        </svg>
                        <span>@Loc["CancelFormHeading"] <strong>@CultureFormat.FormatDigits(_sale.DisplayNumber)</strong></span>
                    </div>
                    <label class="m-cancel-form-label" for="cancel-reason">@Loc["CancelFormReasonLabel"]</label>
                    <textarea id="cancel-reason"
                              class="m-cancel-form-textarea"
                              rows="3"
                              placeholder="@Loc["CancelFormReasonPlaceholder"]"
                              @bind="_cancellationReason"
                              @bind:event="oninput"
                              disabled="@_isBusy">
                    </textarea>
                    <div class="m-cancel-form-btns">
                        <button type="button"
                                class="m-btn m-btn-danger m-btn-block"
                                disabled="@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_cancellationReason) || _isBusy)"
                                @onclick="ExecuteCancellation">
                            @(_isBusy ? Loc["CancelFormCancelling"] : Loc["CancelFormConfirm"])
                        </button>
                        <button type="button"
                                class="m-btn m-btn-secondary m-btn-block"
                                disabled="@_isBusy"
                                @onclick="HideCancelForm">
                            @Loc["CancelFormDiscard"]
                        </button>
                    </div>
                </div>
            }
            else
            {
                @if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Pending))
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="m-btn m-btn-primary m-btn-block"
                            disabled="@_isBusy"
                            @onclick="HandleApproveAsync">
                        @(_isBusy ? Loc["ActionWorking"] : Loc["ActionApprove"])
                    </button>
                }
                @if (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Approved))
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="m-btn m-btn-gold m-btn-block"
                            disabled="@_isBusy"
                            @onclick="HandleMarkInvoicedAsync">
                        @(_isBusy ? Loc["ActionWorking"] : Loc["ActionMarkInvoiced"])
                    </button>
                }
                @if (_canCancel)
                {
                    <button type="button"
                            class="m-btn m-btn-danger m-btn-block"
                            disabled="@_isBusy"
                            @onclick="ShowCancelForm">
                        @Loc["ActionCancel"]
                    </button>
                }
            }

            <button type="button"
                    class="m-btn m-btn-secondary m-btn-block"
                    disabled="@_isBusy"
                    @onclick="GoToSales">
                @Loc["BackToList"]
            </button>
        </div>
    }

    @* ── 8. Footer — version string *@
    <div class="m-footer">
        @Loc["Version"]
    </div>
}

@code {
    // ── Route parameter ────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Sale Id from the URL. The @page constraint `{SaleId:guid}` ensures
    /// only valid Guid strings reach this parameter; malformed URLs hit the
    /// router's NotFound template instead.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Guid SaleId { get; set; }

    // ── State ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private SaleDto? _sale;
    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the current user is in Employee, Manager, or Admin role
    /// (matches the [RequireRoles] on ApproveSaleCommand, MarkAsInvoicedCommand,
    /// CancelSaleCommand). Computed synchronously in OnInitializedAsync from
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider so the action-stack visibility doesn't
    /// flicker on first render. ReadOnly + Customer roles can view but not act.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canActOnSales;

    /// <summary>
    /// True while an action (Approve / MarkInvoiced / Cancel) is in flight.
    /// Disables all action buttons + the cancel form's Confirm/Discard to
    /// prevent double-clicks and concurrent command dispatch.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isBusy;

    /// <summary>
    /// Inline error message for the action panel. Populated when an action
    /// fails (e.g. insufficient stock). Cleared on the next successful
    /// action or when the user opens the inline cancel form.
    /// </summary>
    private string _actionError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// True when the inline cancel form is open in the action panel.
    /// Mutated by ShowCancelForm / HideCancelForm.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _showCancelForm;

    /// <summary>
    /// Bound to the textarea in the inline cancel form. Trimmed and
    /// length-validated (3-500 chars) before dispatch.
    /// </summary>
    private string _cancellationReason = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// True if the sale is in a cancellable state (Pending or Approved).
    /// Drafts are cancellable via DeleteDraftSaleCommand (handled on /m/Cart);
    /// Invoiced sales require a credit note flow (not implemented in v1).
    /// Computed from _sale.Status after the load succeeds.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _canCancel =>
        _sale is not null
        && (_sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Pending) || _sale.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Approved));

    // ── Lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Resolve _canActOnSales synchronously via AuthStateProvider so the
        // action stack doesn't flicker on first render. NOTE: we deliberately
        // do NOT use ICurrentUserService.IsInRole here — in interactive Blazor
        // Server mode, ICurrentUserService resolves from
        // IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext, which is null over the SignalR
        // circuit (only populated during the initial prerender). The
        // AuthStateProvider is the canonical source for interactive
        // components. The Wolverine command handlers also enforce
        // [RequireRoles] server-side as defense-in-depth.
        var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
        var user = authState.User;
        _canActOnSales = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin)
                         || user.IsInRole(Roles.Manager)
                         || user.IsInRole(Roles.Employee);

        try
        {
            await LoadSaleAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadSaleAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            await LoadSaleCoreAsync();
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Silent-reload variant used by ExecuteActionAsync after a successful
    /// action. Skips toggling _isLoading so the page doesn't flash the
    /// full-page loading spinner between a successful action and the
    /// refreshed content (mirrors the desktop SaleDetail.razor pattern).
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync()
    {
        // NOTE: do NOT touch _isLoading here — that would blank the page
        // with the loading spinner. We keep _isBusy = true (set by the
        // caller ExecuteActionAsync) so action buttons stay disabled while
        // the reload is in flight.
        try
        {
            await LoadSaleCoreAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Silent-reload failures are non-fatal — the action itself
            // already succeeded and we already toasted success. The next
            // user interaction (or a manual page refresh) will surface
            // any persistent load failure via the regular LoadSaleAsync
            // path.
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Shared core for both LoadSaleAsync (initial load + retry) and
    /// ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync (post-action refresh). Sets _sale + _loadError.
    /// Does NOT touch _isLoading — that's the caller's responsibility.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task LoadSaleCoreAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var query = new GetSaleByIdQuery { SaleId = SaleId };
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<SaleDto>>(query);

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _sale = result.Value;
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error contains the handler's user-friendly message.
                // For "not found" (covers both genuinely-missing AND
                // permission-denied), we show the same NotFound UI.
                _loadError = result.Error ?? Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
                _sale = null;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_GenericLoad"];
            _sale = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Staff actions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleApproveAsync()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;

        // Defensive: button is rendered only when status == Pending, but the
        // handler also enforces this. Belt-and-suspenders.
        if (_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Pending)) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionApprove"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new ApproveSaleCommand(_sale.Id)));
    }

    private async Task HandleMarkInvoicedAsync()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;

        if (_sale.Status != nameof(SaleStatus.Approved)) return;

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionMarkInvoiced"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new MarkAsInvoicedCommand(_sale.Id)));
    }

    // ── Cancel flow (inline two-step, mirrors MobileCart's _confirmingClear) ──
    //
    // Step 1: User clicks "Cancel order" → ShowCancelForm() flips
    //         _showCancelForm to true, which renders the inline cancel form
    //         (textarea + Discard/Confirm buttons) in place of the action
    //         buttons.
    // Step 2: User enters a reason and clicks "Confirm Cancellation" →
    //         ExecuteCancellation() validates the reason length client-side
    //         (3-500 chars, matching CancelSaleCommandValidator — defense-
    //         in-depth) and dispatches CancelSaleCommand via Wolverine. On
    //         success the inline form is hidden and the sale is silently
    //         reloaded to refresh the status banner + audit trail.

    /// <summary>
    /// Step 1 — opens the inline cancel form. Does NOT dispatch any command.
    /// </summary>
    private void ShowCancelForm()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;
        if (!_canCancel) return;

        _showCancelForm = true;
        _actionError = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Closes the inline cancel form and clears the entered reason. Called
    /// when the user clicks "Discard" in the form, or after a successful
    /// cancellation (so the form doesn't stay open over a now-cancelled sale).
    /// </summary>
    private void HideCancelForm()
    {
        _showCancelForm = false;
        _cancellationReason = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Step 2 — dispatches CancelSaleCommand. Validates the reason length
    /// client-side first (3-500 chars, matches CancelSaleCommandValidator).
    /// Reuses ExecuteActionAsync for the busy-state / error / success /
    /// reload flow. After success, hides the inline form so the user sees
    /// the cancelled state without the form still being open.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ExecuteCancellation()
    {
        if (_sale is null || _isBusy) return;

        var reason = (_cancellationReason ?? string.Empty).Trim();

        // Client-side validation: 3-500 chars (matches CancelSaleCommandValidator).
        if (reason.Length < 3 || reason.Length > 500)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["CancelReasonLengthError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        await ExecuteActionAsync(
            Loc["ActionCancel"],
            () => MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(new CancelSaleCommand(_sale.Id, reason)));

        // If the action succeeded, ExecuteActionAsync already reloaded the
        // sale. Hide the inline form so the user sees the cancelled state
        // without the form still being open. (On failure we keep the form
        // open so they can retry without re-entering the reason.)
        if (_sale?.Status == nameof(SaleStatus.Cancelled))
        {
            HideCancelForm();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Translates stable, culture-neutral error codes (returned by the
    /// Approve / MarkAsInvoiced / Cancel command handlers) into culture-
    /// aware messages for the current UI culture. Returns null for any
    /// error string it doesn't recognize — the caller falls back to the raw
    /// error or to Error_GenericAction. Mirrors the desktop SaleDetail.razor
    /// LocalizeError helper verbatim so both pages share a consistent
    /// localization strategy for command-handler errors.
    /// </summary>
    private string? LocalizeError(string? error)
    {
        if (StockErrors.TryParse(error, out var stockName, out var stock, out var required))
        {
            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["StockExceeded"],
                stockName,
                stock,
                required);
        }
        if (CategoryDeactivatedErrors.TryParse(error, out var deactivatedName))
        {
            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["CategoryDeactivated"],
                deactivatedName);
        }
        if (PurchaseLimitErrors.TryParse(error, out var limitName, out var limit))
        {
            return string.Format(
                CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
                Loc["PurchaseLimitExceeded"],
                limitName,
                limit);
        }
        // NoCustomerGroup is produced when the customer on the sale has no
        // CustomerGroup assigned. The backend rejects the mutation outright.
        // The localized message tells the staff user to assign the customer
        // to a group before adding more items.
        if (NoCustomerGroupErrors.TryParse(error))
        {
            return Loc["NoCustomerGroup"];
        }
        return null;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Common wrapper for the three staff actions: sets _isBusy, clears the
    /// previous _actionError, dispatches the command, handles success
    /// (toast + silent reload to refresh status banner + audit trail +
    /// action-button enabled states) and failure (inline _actionError banner
    /// + error toast). Mirrors the desktop SaleDetail.razor pattern.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ExecuteActionAsync(string actionName, Func<Task<Result>> dispatch)
    {
        _isBusy = true;
        _actionError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var result = await dispatch();

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActionSuccessFormat"], actionName),
                    summary: Loc["ActionSuccessTitle"]);

                // Reload the sale to refresh the status banner, audit trail,
                // and action-button enabled states. Uses the SILENT reload
                // (not LoadSaleAsync) so the page doesn't flash the full-page
                // loading spinner between the toast and the refreshed content.
                // _isBusy stays true here (set at the top of this method) so
                // action buttons remain disabled during the reload.
                await ReloadSaleSilentlyAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // result.Error may be a stable, culture-neutral error code
                // (e.g. StockErrors.Format / CategoryDeactivatedErrors.Format /
                // PurchaseLimitErrors.Format / NoCustomerGroupErrors.Format)
                // that needs to be localized into the user's language.
                // LocalizeError returns null for errors it doesn't recognize —
                // we fall back to the raw error string, or to Error_GenericAction
                // if the handler returned no error.
                _actionError = LocalizeError(result.Error) ?? Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
                await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _actionError = Loc["Error_GenericAction"];
            await Toast.Error(_actionError, summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusy = false;
        }
    }

